## Objective
- Autonomously bug-hunt `sptpub.com` (from `data/targets.txt`) per `skills/AGENT.md`: enumerate subdomains, discover routes/APIs, test client- and server-side, create two test accounts if possible, and report valid impactful vulns in `result/`.
- Must never ask the user questions; act as a top bug bounty hunter; only report confirmed, practical, high-impact findings.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn`; HEAD `6560caa`; run_id `40885570838`; target-state `decision=reset` (target hash changed); `target_hash=8469afc002cedac143955328ae992842f864c4bb9f05b8e80bde0d4c1750b946`.
- Tooling verified: node v22.23.4, python 3.14.4, Chrome 156 headless CDP at `127.0.0.1:9222`, curl, git, dig; `chrome-devtools` MCP works.
- `creds/test-account.txt` is for `console.byteplus.com` — NOT in scope for `sptpub.com`; do not use.
- Scope per user instruction: `sptpub.com` + discovered `*.sptpub.com` subdomains; harmless/read-only testing only. Out of scope: `sptpub-infra.com` (sibling), brand external domains, CloudFront/AWS/S3 infrastructure itself, and non-sptpub buckets (i.e., do not probe `spt77-dynamic-files` etc.).
- Target is a multi-tenant betting white-label platform (brands: bettilt, blaze, joycasino, bcgame, etc.) with per-tenant `api-*` CloudFront hosts.
- 259 subdomains discovered (subdomain.center + hackertarget + rapiddns), saved to `result/inventory/subdomains.txt`; only 27 resolve; 208 are `api-*`.
- ALL dynamic hosts are edge-blocked from this network vantage: brands return `403` JSON `{ "error": "access blocked" }`; `api-*` return `503` with header `bb-rsn: bc`; `api-help-beta`/`help-beta`/`api1-ws` return CloudFront generic 403 HTML. Block persists across methods, paths, headers, browser UA, and real Chrome — geo/ASN/bot block.
- `api.sptpub.com` (159.69.41.140/141 Hetzner) and `help`/`wiki` (88.208.6.60/61 Fasthosts) time out / ports closed. No IPv6 egress.
- Account creation impossible (app blocked); must document and fall back to unauthenticated only.
- Reachable only: S3 static buckets (public listing), no sensitive data:
  - `static.sptpub.com` → bucket `spt77-static` (eu-central-1, CloudFront `d1bvoel1nv172p.cloudfront.net`); listing = `404.html` + `additional_images/background/*.png`; CloudFront strips query strings so no pagination.
  - `files-immutable-4cbc033nbd3.sptpub.com` → bucket `spt77-nondynamic-files`; prefixes: `currencies/` (2), `flags_by_code/` (62365), `rocket-league/` (2), `translations/` (55 market-tooltip i18n JSON). ACL: AllUsers `READ` + `READ_ACP`, NO write; policy read denied.
  - `bt-app-static-themes.sptpub.com` denies all objects (403).
- `help-beta-ingress.sptpub.com` CNAMEs to deleted ELB `a07ff76e120d64a249d5504f3705266f-1179737841.eu-central-1.elb.amazonaws.com` (NXDOMAIN); not claimable/takeover (account-bound).
- `dragonclub.sptpub.com` → `robuvboqwvihfwe983bcae.sptpub-infra.com` (active Route53, not dangling, out-of-scope target).
- No confirmed high-impact vulnerabilities found so far.

